<title>USA: High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</title>
<headline>High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>High cotton prices triggered a seventeenth special quota permitting entry of 44,983,440 kg (99,171,591 lb) of upland cotton, USDA said Thursday.</p>
<p>The quota, to be established December 21, applies to cotton bought no later than March 20, 1997, and entered into the United States not later than June 18, 1997.</p>
</text>
